INSERT INTO `studentcornerdetail` VALUES (1,'National Defence University (Islamabad)',1,'The President of Pakistan is the Chancellor of the NDU. The management of the NDU is vested in a three Star General from the Pakistan Army, who is called the President of the University. The University is organized into two Faculties and one',1,0,'studentcorner/SC1-ndu815133853.jpg','','http://www.ndu.edu.pk/',5),(3,'National University  of Sciences & Technology (Islamabad)',1,'National University of Sciences and Technology (NUST) is a premier national institution that has won global acclaim within a short span of time. Various constituent schools and colleges functioning under the umbrella of NUST are imparting high',1,0,'studentcorner/SC3-nust450028400.jpg','','http://www.nust.edu.pk/',5),(4,'Riphah International University (Islamabad)',1,'Riphah International University was established by Islamic International Medical College Trust (IIMCT) to impart research oriented professional education with the focus on inculcation of Islamic ethical values. The university was chartered by ',1,0,'studentcorner/SC4-riphah1380502281.jpg','','http://www.riphah.edu.pk/',5),(5,'Quaid-i-Azam University (Islamabad)',1,'Quaid-i-Azam University (once named Islamabad University) was established in July 1967 under the Act of National Assembly and started teaching and research programmes for PhD and MPhil degrees. It was, however, gradually and later decided to',1,0,'studentcorner/SC5-qau334687157.jpg','','http://www.qau.edu.pk/',5),(6,'University of Aberdeen, Scotland',2,'The University of Aberdeen is today at the forefront of teaching, learning and discovery, as it has been for 500 years. As the \'global university of the north\', we have consistently sent pioneers and ideas outward to every part of the world.\r\n',1,0,'studentcorner/SC6-aberdeen_uni11191521985.jpg','',' http://www.abdn.ac.uk/',5),(7,'Abertay University Dundee, Scotland ',2,'As a university we are immensely proud of our academic achievements but there is a great deal more to us. We are a modern new university, one with a long history and have quickly become one of Scotland\'s leading universities, highly ranked for',1,0,'studentcorner/SC7-abertay683100139.jpg','','http://www.abertay.ac.uk/',5),(8,'Anglia Ruskin University ',2,'Anglia Ruskin University was awarded university status in 1992. Today, with a student population of 31,000, we are one of the largest universities in the East of England, and a large provider of part-time education. Our students are on ',1,0,'studentcorner/SC8-anglia_ruskin417858728.jpg','','http://www.anglia.ac.uk/',5),(9,'University of the Arts, London ',2,'University of the Arts London welcomes students and teachers from more than 100 countries and around 40 per cent of our students come from outside the UK. Such a diverse mix of individuals creates an extremely vibrant learning environment ',1,0,'studentcorner/SC9-ual591619229.jpg','','http://www.arts.ac.uk/',5),(10,'Aston University, Birmingham ',2,'Founded in 1895 and a University since 1966, Aston is a long established research-led University known for its world-class teaching quality and strong links to industry, government and commerce. Professor Dame Julia King became Vice-Chancellor ',1,0,'studentcorner/SC10-aston_uni1376342463.jpg','','http://www1.aston.ac.uk/',5),(11,'Bangor University, Bangor',2,'An assessment by the UK Publishing Group ResearchResearch named Bangor as one of a handful of UK universities whose research progress was outstanding, while the latest RAE confirmed that world leading research is being carried out across \r\n',1,0,'studentcorner/SC11-bangor_uni785521332.jpg','','http://www.bangor.ac.uk/',5),(12,'Pakistan Institute of Development Economics (Islamabad)',1,'The Pakistan Institute of Development Economics is located at the Quaid-i-Azam University Campus in Islamabad. The campus rests against the backdrop of the Margalla hills on the Potohar Plateau, within a short distance of the remains of Taxila,\r\n',1,0,'studentcorner/SC12-pide687609319.jpg','',' http://www.pide.org.pk/',5),(13,'Pakistan Institute of Engineering & Applied Sciences (Islamabad)',1,'The institute has a strong faculty of highly qualified scientists, engineers in the diverse fields of physical sciences, engineering and medicine. The total strength of the full-time faculty at present is 90, representing a wide variety of ',1,0,'studentcorner/SC13-a_pieas1464683622.jpg','','http://www.pieas.edu.pk/',5),(14,'National University of Modern Languages (Islamabad)',1,'The National University of Modern Languages was established as an institute in 1970 to help people communicate and understand each other in different oriental and occidental languages, to assimilate different cultures and to act as',1,0,'studentcorner/SC14-numl783648532.jpg','','http://www.numl.edu.pk/',5),(15,' National University of Computer & Emerging Sciences (Islamabad)',1,'The National University of Computer & Emerging Sciences has the honor of being the first multi-campus private sector university set up under the Federal Charter granted by Ordinance No.XXIII of 2000, dated July 01, 2000.	The University ',1,0,'studentcorner/SC15-nu1920138678.jpg','','http://www.nu.edu.pk/',5),(16,' International Islamic University (Islamabad)',1,'To develop an international Islamic seat of higher learning, research instruction and training in various branches of knowledge with special emphasis on Islamic Studies, Social Sciences and humanities to be taught, studied, developed and',1,0,'studentcorner/SC16-iiu1417200263.jpg','','http://www.iiu.edu.pk/',5),(17,'Institute of Space Technology (Islamabad)',1,'The past century has been host to many technological advancements resulting in a gradual progression towards the betterment of society. Space science as such, has been a vital force behind this advancement and has revolutionalized the',1,0,'studentcorner/SC17-ist1876888739.jpg','','http://www.ist.edu.pk/',5),(18,'Foundation University (Islamabad)',1,'The Foundation University Islamabad (FUI) has been established as a private sector university. It is sponsored by the Fauji Foundation which is the largest welfare organization in the country having vast human and financial resources.The ',1,0,'studentcorner/SC18-fui569653394.jpg','','http://www.fui.edu.pk/',5),(19,'Federal Urdu University of Arts, Sciences & Technology (Islamabad)',1,'The Federal Urdu University of Arts, Sciences & Technology enjoys the unique distinction of being the first ever university in Pakistan, which ultimately aims at using Urdu as the main language of instruction and teachingâ€¦\r\n',1,0,'studentcorner/SC19-fuuast1926975290.jpg','',' http://www.fuuast.edu.pk/',5),(20,'COMSATS Institute of Information Technology (Islamabad)',1,'The COMSATS Institute of Information Technology envisions assuming a truly national character for itself in the year to come. It envisions having presence in all provinces of the country. It sees for itself a position among the top five (5)',1,0,'studentcorner/SC20-ciit1824793358.jpg','','http://ciit-isb.edu.pk/',5),(21,'Bahria University (Islamabad)',1,'Pakistan Navy established Bahria Institute at Islamabad and Karachi in the late eighties. These Institutes were aimed at providing quality and uninterrupted education up to Intermediate level, to the children of naval personnel on their ',1,0,'studentcorner/SC21-bui1272396012.jpg','','http://bui.edu.pk/',5),(22,'Allama Iqbal Open University (Islamabad)',1,'Allama Iqbal Open University (AIOU) is the first Open University in Asia. AIOU is a unique institution in Pakistan because of its philosophy, system, approach, functions and overall structure. The University with its main campus at Islamabad',1,0,'studentcorner/SC22-aiou1661347569.jpg','',' http://www.aiou.edu.pk/',5),(23,' Air University (Islamabad)',1,'The mission of Air University is to achieve excellence in teaching and research for producing graduates with sound professional knowledge, integrity of character, a keen sense of social responsibility and a passion for lifelong learning.   ',1,0,'studentcorner/SC23-air_university_logo1488008513.jpg','',' http://www.au.edu.pk/',5),(24,' University of Bath',2,'The University of Bath was granted university status in 1966 by Royal Charter, however our roots can be traced back to the Bristol Trade School - a technical school established in 1856. In 1885 the school was renamed the Merchant Venturers\' ',1,0,'studentcorner/SC24-bath_uni1988283525.jpg','','http://www.bath.ac.uk/',5),(25,'University of Bedfordshire ',2,'University of Bedfordshire graduates enjoy excellent employment rates, with 90% in work or further study within six months of graduating (Destination of Leavers from Higher Education Survey 2010). More than three-quarters of students at the \r\n',1,0,'studentcorner/SC25-bedford_uni1196927495.jpg','',' http://www.beds.ac.uk/',5),(26,' Bath Spa University ',2,'Why Study at Bath Spa University: From its rich history and beautiful settings, to its diverse course offering and the people who make up the team, we could probably come up with hundreds of reasons to choose Bath Spa University, but here ',1,0,'studentcorner/SC26-bathspa_uni1697525448.jpg','','http://www.bathspa.ac.uk/',5),(27,'University of Birmingham ',2,'The University was founded in 1900 on an anti-discrimination ethos accepting men and women on an equal basis. Today, as a community of over 145 nationalities in one of the UKâ€™s most vibrant cities, we remain committed to promoting equality, ',1,0,'studentcorner/SC27-birmingham_uni1108491902.jpg','',' http://www.birmingham.ac.uk/',5),(28,'Birmingham City University ',2,'A degree from Birmingham City University is a passport to a successful future. From the Â£180 million investment in our facilities to our great links with leading employers, we provide our students with the skills they need to succeed.',1,0,'studentcorner/SC28-birmingham_city_uni62834341.jpg','','http://www.bcu.ac.uk/',5),(29,